.SH "struct pdg::MouseEvent"
.PP 
\fBMouseEvent\fP\&. 

the user did something with the mouse

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Documentation-only JavaScript shape, not a runtime constructor\&.
.RE
.PP
 
.PP
\fBFields\fP
.RS 4
Field  Type  Required/default  Meaning  alt  \fRboolean\fP  Required  buttonNumber  \fRnumber\fP  Required  ctrl  \fRboolean\fP  Required  emitter  \fR\fBEventEmitter\fP\fP  Required  eventType  \fRnumber\fP  Required  lastClickElapsed  \fRnumber\fP  Required  lastClickPos  \fR\fBPoint\fP\fP  Required  leftButton  \fRboolean\fP  Required  meta  \fRboolean\fP  Required  mousePos  \fR\fBPoint\fP\fP  Required  rightButton  \fRboolean\fP  Required  shift  \fRboolean\fP  Required  
.RE
.PP
Generated by the \fBEventManager\fP whenever the user moves the mouse (\fBpdg\&.eventType_MouseMove\fP) or clicks a mouse button (\fBpdg\&.eventType_MouseDown\fP and \fBpdg\&.eventType_MouseUp\fP)\&.

.PP
The \fBEventManager\fP also tracks the state of the mouse buttons, so you can retrieve that at any time with \fBpdg\&.EventManager\&.isButtonDown()\fP\&. The \fBGraphicsManager\fP tracks the position of the mouse, and that can be retrieved at any time with \fBpdg\&.GraphicsManager\&.getMouse()\fP\&. 
.PP
.nf
{ 
    emitter: {},            // the emitter that generated this event
    eventType: 7,           // the event type (eventType_MouseUp|Down|Move)
    shift: false,           // true if the shift key is held down
    ctrl: false,            // true if the control key is held down
    alt: false,             // true if the alt (or option) key is held down
    meta: false,            // true if the meta (windows or command) key is held down
    mousePos: {
        x: 456,                         // the x coordinate of the mouse when the event occurred
        y: 201              // the y coordinate of the mouse when the event occurred
    },
    leftButton: false,      // true if the left mouse button was down
    rightButton: false,     // true if the right mouse button was down
    buttonNumber: 0,        // button number (0=left, 1=right, 2=middle) or finger ID for touch
    lastClickPos: { 
        x: 456,                         // the x coordinate of the last mouseDown event
        y: 201              // the y coordinate of the last mouseDown event
    },
    lastClickElapsed: 201   // the number of milliseconds since the last mouseDown
}

.fi
.PP

.PP
Location and time since the last mouseDown event are provided to make it easier to detect double-clicks, dragging, and gestures\&.

.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
on a touch device mouse moved events are only generated when the user is touching the device, and each finger touching is treated like a separate mouse button, with the button number based on the order the fingers touched the device\&.

.PP
A \fBSpriteLayer\fP has the ability to automatically handle these mouse events and generate \fBpdg\&.eventType_SpriteTouch\fP for any \fBSprite\fP that was clicked on, or pass these on as mouse events if no \fBSprite\fP was hit\&.
.RE
.PP
